.TH OTPME-SHARE 1 "2025-12-29" "OTPme 0.3.0a120" "OTPme Manual"
.SH NAME
otpme-share \- manage OTPme file shares
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpme-share
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIshare\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otpme-share
manages file shares in the OTPme system. A share provides access to a directory tree and can optionally be encrypted.
.PP
Shares support two types of scripts: An \fBadd script\fR (default: add_share.sh) is automatically executed when a share is created to set up the share directory structure. A \fBmount script\fR (default: mount_share.sh) can be configured to run each time a user mounts the share. Scripts are executed as the OTPme system user and group. The default scripts for new shares can be configured via the \fBdefault_share_add_script\fR and \fBdefault_share_mount_script\fR config parameters at site or unit level.
.SH HOME SHARES
A normal share hands out its root directory to everybody. A \fBhome share\fR hands out \fIshare_root\fB/\fIhome_dir\fR instead, so every user gets their own directory and sees nothing else. The directory is created on the first mount, owned by the user and by default with mode 0700 (see \fBhome_share_permissions\fR).
.PP
Two naming schemes are available, chosen when the share is created:
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-home\-share
The directory is named after the user UUID. Renaming a user keeps the directory.
.TP
.B \-\-home\-share\-uid
The directory is named after the user name (uid), which is what one expects below e.g. /home. Implies \fB\-\-home\-share\fR.
.RE
.PP
A \fBroot mount token\fR gets no home dir and mounts \fIshare_root\fR itself, so it reaches the home dirs of all users (see \fBadd_root_mount_token\fR).
.PP
Home shares can be encrypted. Every home dir is then encrypted on its own, with a share key per user, which is why an encrypted home share has no root mount token.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Share Management
.TP
.B add \fR[\fB\-\-home\-share\fR] [\fB\-\-home\-share\-uid\fR] [\fB\-\-force\-group\fR \fIgroup\fR] [\fB\-\-force\-directory\-mode\fR \fImode\fR] [\fB\-\-force\-create\-mode\fR \fImode\fR] [\fB\-\-crypt\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-key\-gen\fR] [\fB\-\-block\-size\fR \fIsize\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-len\fR \fIlen\fR] [\fB\-\-restore\fR \fIrestore_share\fR] [\fB\-\-restore\-token\fR \fItoken\fR] \fIshare\fR
Create a new share. Use \fB\-\-force\-group\fR to set forced group, \fB\-\-force\-directory\-mode\fR and \fB\-\-force\-create\-mode\fR to set permissions for new directories and files. Use \fB\-\-crypt\fR to enable encryption, \fB\-\-restore\fR to add a restore share and \fB\-\-restore\-token\fR for encrypted restore shares.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-home\-share
Create a home share (see \fBHOME SHARES\fR above). Each user gets their own subdirectory, named after the user UUID.
.TP
.B \-\-home\-share\-uid
Create a home share whose subdirectories are named after the user name (uid) instead of the user UUID. Implies \fB\-\-home\-share\fR.
.RE
.TP
.B del \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-persist\-mount\fR|\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIshare\fR
Delete a share. Asks for confirmation according to the confirmation policy, and warns about assigned tokens and roles. For an encrypted share it also warns that the share keys are deleted with it, so its data can then only be decrypted by someone in possession of the master password. Online hosts are told to unmount the share.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send unmount notification to all online hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send unmount notification to all online hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-persist\-mount
Also remove persisted share mounts on hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Keep persisted share mounts on hosts (transient unmount only).
.RE
.TP
.B show \fR[\fIshare\fR]
Display share information.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIregex\fR]
List shares, optionally filtered by regex pattern.
.TP
.B enable \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-persist\-mount\fR|\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIshare\fR
Enable a disabled share.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-persist\-mount
Persist new share mounts on hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Do not persist new share mounts on hosts.
.RE
.TP
.B disable \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-persist\-mount\fR|\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIshare\fR
Disable a share without deleting it.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-persist\-mount
Also remove persisted share mounts on hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Keep persisted share mounts on hosts (transient unmount only).
.RE
.TP
.B rename \fIshare\fR \fInew_name\fR
Rename a share.
.TP
.B move \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-acls\fR] \fIshare\fR \fIunit\fR
Move share to a different unit.
.TP
.B touch \fIshare\fR
Re-index the object to fix potential index problems.
.SS Share Configuration
.TP
.B root_dir \fIshare\fR \fIpath\fR
Set the share root directory.
.TP
.B force_group \fIshare\fR \fIgroup\fR
Files and directories will always be owned by the given group.
.TP
.B force_create_mode \fIshare\fR \fImode\fR
Set file creation mode.
.TP
.B force_directory_mode \fIshare\fR \fImode\fR
Set directory creation mode.
.TP
.B home_share_permissions \fIshare\fR \fImode\fR
Mode the per user directories of a home share are created with, in python format (e.g. \fB0o750\fR). The default \fB0o700\fR keeps the users out of each others home dirs.
.TP
.B enable_ro \fIshare\fR
Make share read-only.
.TP
.B disable_ro \fIshare\fR
Make share read-write.
.TP
.B description \fIshare\fR \fR[\fIdescription\fR]
Set share description.
.TP
.B info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIshare\fR \fR[\fIinfo\fR]
Set free-form info text. If \fIinfo\fR is omitted, the current info text is
opened in the editor specified by the \fBEDITOR\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B dump_info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIshare\fR
Dump the info text to stdout.
.SS Mount Script
A mount script is executed each time the share is mounted by a user. It can be used to perform custom actions during mount, such as preparing the share directory or checking prerequisites. The mount script must be enabled separately after being configured.
.TP
.B mount_script \fIshare\fR \fImount_script\fR \fR[\fB\-\-\fR \fIscript_options\fR]
Change share mount script.
.TP
.B enable_mount_script \fIshare\fR
Enable share mount script.
.TP
.B disable_mount_script \fIshare\fR
Disable share mount script.
.SS Encryption
.TP
.B get_share_key \fIshare\fR \fIuser\fR
Get encrypted share key for a user.
.SS SOTP Signing
With SOTP signing enabled a client has to sign the SOTP it authenticates with using the users sign private key. The share stores a copy of the sign public key of every user that has a token assigned, and the node verifies the signature against that copy. This keeps a user of another site from getting access with an SOTP alone: whoever controls the nodes of that site can produce a valid SOTP and can change the users public key there, but cannot touch the copy inside the share. Shares with SOTP signing do not support roles, because a role would bring in tokens whose users sign public keys are missing.
.TP
.B enable_sotp_signing \fIshare\fR
Require clients to sign the SOTP they authenticate with. Only possible if no role is assigned to the share and all users with a token assigned have a sign public key. Their keys are copied into the share.
.TP
.B disable_sotp_signing \fIshare\fR
Do no longer require clients to sign their SOTP. The sign public keys stored in the share are removed with it.
.TP
.B update_sign_public_keys \fIshare\fR \fR[\fIusername\fR]
Take over the current sign public keys of the users that have a token assigned, for all of them or only for \fIusername\fR. A user who generates a new key pair loses access until this is run, which is on purpose: updating the copy automatically would hand the users site the control over it that the copy is meant to take away. Keys of users without a token on the share are removed.
.SS Token and Role Management
.TP
.B add_token \fIshare\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Add a token to the share. With SOTP signing enabled the sign public key of the tokens user is stored in the share.
.TP
.B remove_token \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-share\-key\fR|\fB\-\-remove\-share\-key\fR] \fIshare\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Remove a token from the share. The users sign public key is removed with their last token, like the share key of an encrypted share. On an encrypted share, \fB\-\-keep\-share\-key\fR retains the user's share key even after their last token is removed; \fB\-\-remove\-share\-key\fR forces removal immediately.
.TP
.B list_tokens \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIshare\fR
List tokens assigned to the share. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.TP
.B add_role \fIshare\fR \fIrole\fR
Add a role to the share. Not supported by encrypted shares and by shares with SOTP signing enabled.
.TP
.B remove_role \fIshare\fR \fIrole\fR
Remove a role from the share.
.TP
.B list_roles \fR[\fB\-r\fR] \fIshare\fR
List roles assigned to the share. Use \fB\-r\fR for recursive listing.
.TP
.B list_users \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIshare\fR
List users of the share. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS Host Management
.TP
.B add_host \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] [\fB\-\-persist\-mount\fR|\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIshare\fR \fIhost\fR
Add a host to the share.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-persist\-mount
Persist new share mounts on hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Do not persist new share mounts on hosts.
.RE
.TP
.B remove_host \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] [\fB\-\-persist\-mount\fR|\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIshare\fR \fIhost\fR
Remove a host from the share.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-persist\-mount
Also remove persisted share mounts on hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Keep persisted share mounts on hosts (transient unmount only).
.RE
.TP
.B list_hosts \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIshare\fR
List hosts assigned to the share. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.TP
.B add_group \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] [\fB\-\-persist\-mount\fR|\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIshare\fR \fIgroup\fR
Add a (host) group to the share. Every host in the group inherits the share assignment.
.TP
.B remove_group \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] [\fB\-\-persist\-mount\fR|\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIshare\fR \fIgroup\fR
Remove a host group from the share.
.TP
.B list_groups \fIshare\fR
List host groups assigned to the share.
.TP
.B mount_timeout \fIshare\fR \fR[\fItimeout\fR]
Set the idle timeout after which a mount drops its unused connection. \fB0\fR disables the timeout (the connection stays open as long as the mount does).
.TP
.B limit_hosts \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] [\fB\-\-persist\-mount\fR|\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIshare\fR
Limit share access to assigned hosts and host groups.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-persist\-mount
Also remove persisted share mounts on hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Keep persisted share mounts on hosts (transient unmount only).
.RE
.TP
.B unlimit_hosts \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] [\fB\-\-persist\-mount\fR|\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIshare\fR
Remove host-based access limitation on the share.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-persist\-mount
Persist new share mounts on hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Do not persist new share mounts on hosts.
.RE
.SS Master Password Token
.TP
.B add_master_password_token \fIshare\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Allow a token to mount the share with master password.
.TP
.B remove_master_password_token \fIshare\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Remove a master password token from the share.
.SS Root Mount Token
.PP
A root mount token gets no home dir, it mounts \fIshare_root\fR itself and thus reaches the home dirs of all users (see \fBHOME SHARES\fR above). Only available for unencrypted home shares.
.TP
.B add_root_mount_token \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-persist\-mount\fR|\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIshare\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Let a token mount the share root of a home share. The share root the token gets changes, so the token is told to mount again, like with \fBadd_token\fR.
.TP
.B remove_root_mount_token \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-persist\-mount\fR|\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIshare\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Remove a root mount token from the share. The token is told to unmount, like with \fBremove_token\fR.
.SS No Mount Token
.PP
A no mount token is assigned to the share like a normal token \- its user gets a share key and it may mount the share \- but it does not get the share mounted \fBautomatically\fR. It is left out when the shares are mounted at login, and it gets no \fBshare_mount\fR notification. Mounting by hand with \fBotpme\-mount\fR \fIshare_site\fB/\fIshare_name\fR keeps working.
.PP
Unmount notifications still reach these tokens: they may have mounted the share by hand, and a disabled share or a revoked permission has to unmount there too.
.TP
.B add_no_mount_token \fIshare\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Add a token that does not get the share mounted automatically. Handles the share key like \fBadd_token\fR, so an encrypted share asks the client to re-encrypt the key for the tokens user. No mount notification is sent, there is nothing to mount.
.TP
.B remove_no_mount_token \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-share\-key\fR|\fB\-\-remove\-share\-key\fR] \fIshare\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Remove a no mount token from the share. The users share key is removed with it, unless another of their tokens is still assigned to the share or \fB\-\-keep\-share\-key\fR is given.
.SS Pool and Node Management
.TP
.B add_pool \fIshare\fR \fIpool\fR
Add a pool to the share.
.TP
.B remove_pool \fIshare\fR \fIpool\fR
Remove a pool from the share.
.TP
.B list_pools \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIshare\fR
List pools assigned to the share. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.TP
.B add_node \fIshare\fR \fInode\fR
Add a node to the share.
.TP
.B remove_node \fIshare\fR \fInode\fR
Remove a node from the share.
.TP
.B list_nodes \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIshare\fR
List nodes assigned to the share. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS Policy Management
.TP
.B add_policy \fIshare\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Attach a policy to the share.
.TP
.B remove_policy \fIshare\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Remove a policy from the share.
.TP
.B list_policies \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIshare\fR
List policies attached to the share. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS ACL Management
.TP
.B add_acl \fIshare\fR \fIowner_type\fR \fIowner\fR \fIacl\fR
Add an access control entry.
.TP
.B del_acl \fIshare\fR \fIacl\fR
Remove an access control entry.
.TP
.B show_acls \fIshare\fR
Display all ACLs for the share.
.TP
.B enable_acl_inheritance \fIshare\fR
Enable ACL inheritance from parent objects.
.TP
.B disable_acl_inheritance \fIshare\fR
Disable ACL inheritance.
.SS Object Changelog
.TP
.B changelog \fIshare\fR
Show the object's changelog (chronological list of changes with author, timestamp and optional custom text passed via \fB\-\-changelog\fR).
.TP
.B edit_changelog \fIshare\fR \fIchangelog_id\fR
Open the given changelog entry in the editor named by \fBEDITOR\fR to edit its custom text.
.TP
.B del_changelog \fIshare\fR \fIchangelog_id\fR
Remove a single entry from the object's changelog.
.TP
.B clear_changelog \fIshare\fR
Clear the object's entire changelog.
.SS Import/Export
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR] \fIshare\fR
Export share configuration.
.TP
.B remove_orphans \fIshare\fR
Remove orphaned object references.
.SH OPTIONS
